	(text "NIBBLE CARD REG0 - REGISTER BIT 0: bit 0 of A, B and OUT"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 3.5 3.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "553aa0a6-aaa9-4fd8-b4b0-797954769031")
	)
	(text "Cell: 2N7000 + 47k pull-up (NMOS, see docs/gate-cell.md).  99 transistors, 54 resistors, 3 LEDs, 100 x 100 mm (docs/cards.md).\nFrom the bus header: BUS0# (data, active low), CLK, and the control lines AI AO BI BO BA AB OI (docs/isa.md).\nTo the bus header: A0 and B0 (for the ALU and the panel); BUS0# driven open-drain when AO or BO.\nEach register bit is a master-slave D flip-flop. The card's own two-phase clock (PH1, PH2) makes the masters transparent while CLK is low\nand copies them to the slaves on the rising edge. In front of each flip-flop an AND-OR mux selects: A <- bus (AI), B (AB) or hold; B <- bus (BI), A (BA) or hold; OUT <- bus (OI) or hold.\nAB and BA together exchange A and B in one clock. A, B and OUT have no reset. The four bit cards are this design with the bit baked in."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 45.72 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.6 1.6)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "d9251a39-006b-4a05-b5cb-c6cc3bb070f6")
	)
	(text "TWO-PHASE CLOCK (one per card): PH1 = NOR(CLK, PH2) opens the masters while CLK is low, PH2 = NOR(CLKN, PH1) opens the slaves while CLK is high.  The cross-coupling means a phase cannot start rising until the other is fully low, so a flip-flop is never transparent."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 25.4 165.1 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2 2)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "c71ecba9-fd03-464f-bdaa-5a787d203a0d")
	)
